WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.688
Today, there's a deadline
that already passed.

2
00:00:02.688 --> 00:00:06.188
Since September 2025,
domain controllers refuse a

3
00:00:06.188 --> 00:00:09.938
certificate that isn't strongly
mapped to its account.

4
00:00:09.938 --> 00:00:14.781
Microsoft's easy fix, a security
identifier stamped inside the certificate,

5
00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:18.087
only works for certificates
from Microsoft's own CA.

6
00:00:18.087 --> 00:00:22.776
PIV certificates come from the Federal
PKI, so they need a different route.

7
00:00:22.776 --> 00:00:28.238
One is an explicit mapping on each account,
which IDManagement dot gov recommends.

8
00:00:28.238 --> 00:00:31.803
The other is a government-specific
policy Microsoft added,

9
00:00:31.803 --> 00:00:35.513
which trusts name-based mappings
from named federal issuers.

10
00:00:35.513 --> 00:00:37.150
The books now cover both.

11
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:39.460
Next, the coexistence years.
